frv: let the packer see base register updates

frv_registers_update records the registers an insn sets through
note_pattern_stores, which does not report the base register update
of a PRE_MODIFY address (ldu, stu, stbu, ...).  A following insn
that reads the base register was therefore packed into the same VLIW
packet and read the old value:

	stbu.p	gr0, @(gr21,gr4)
	mov	gr21, gr20		; wants gr21 + gr4

Seen as failing strcmp checks in uClibc-ng's tester at -O2.

--- a/gcc/config/frv/frv.cc	2026-10-26 10:45:43.451766816 +0100
+++ b/gcc/config/frv/frv.cc	2026-10-26 10:45:43.672772141 +0100
@@ -7127,6 +7127,13 @@
       x = XEXP (x, 1);
     }
   note_pattern_stores (x, frv_registers_update_1, &flags);
+
+  /* note_pattern_stores does not see the base register update of
+     a load or store with update (ldu, stu, ...).  */
+  subrtx_iterator::array_type array;
+  FOR_EACH_SUBRTX (iter, array, x, NONCONST)
+    if (GET_RTX_CLASS (GET_CODE (*iter)) == RTX_AUTOINC)
+      frv_registers_update_1 (XEXP (*iter, 0), x, &flags);
 }
 
 
